EULER'S TOTIENT FUNCTION
→ 515.8 → Number Theory

φ(n)  —  number of integers k with 1 ≤ k ≤ n and gcd(k, n) = 1

Type:    arithmetic function  n ↦ φ(n)  (n ∈ ℕ)
Variable: n  (positive integer)
Related: Euler's theorem  a^φ(n) ≡ 1 (mod n)  when gcd(a,n)=1
         used to compute RSA private exponent d from public e

FORMULA
φ(n) = n  ∏_{p|n} (1 - 1/p)     p runs over distinct prime factors of n

SPECIAL CASES
prime p:          φ(p) = p - 1          e.g. φ(7) = 6
p^k:              φ(p^k) = p^k - p^{k-1}
multiplicative:   φ(ab) = φ(a)φ(b) when gcd(a,b)=1

EXAMPLE n = 12 = 2²·3
φ(12) = 12 · (1-1/2) · (1-1/3) = 4

        1*
     12     2
  11*         3
 10             4
   9           5*
     8     6
        7*

* = coprime to 12     (1, 5, 7, 11)
    not coprime       (2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10, 12)

MORE VALUES
φ(8)  = 4     φ(10) = 4     φ(11) = 10
more coprimes  →  larger φ(n)

RSA LINK
public modulus N = p·q  (large primes)
φ(N) = (p-1)(q-1)
choose e coprime to φ(N)
private d satisfies  e·d ≡ 1 (mod φ(N))
encryption easy (mod N), inversion hard without factors of N

